2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/202725757/torger-torgerson-wetteland
2 CONT
2 CONT Torger Torgerson Wetteland (1829-1914)
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography:
2 CONT Torger was born in 1829 and was christened on 27 September 1829 in Stavanger Cathedral, Stavanger, Rogaland, Norway. He was the son of Torger Wetteland and Kristine Nedrebo. Torger married Maren Elizabeth Oftedal. In the 1865 cens
2 CONC us for Stavanger, Norway he is living with his wife and their daughter Christine. In the 1885 census Torger is living in Bergen, Norway with the family of his sister Elen Marie. At this same time, his wife and four children: Theod
2 CONC or, Svend, Astrid, and Kristoffer are living in Stavanger. In the Stavnage census it states that Torger is away in Bergen. By this time his oldest daughter Kristine was married and living in the United States. Beathe his second ol
2 CONC dest Beathe also out of the house, probably gone to live with Kristine in Oregon. This might have been a foretelling of things to come. Family stories tell that Torger Wetteland came to America with the family but he later divorce
2 CONC d Maren and returned to Norway to possibly take up with a mistress. It's also reported that Torger helped in the restoration of the Stavanger Cathedral, in Stavanger, Rogaland, Norway by working on artwork, possibly statuary or st
2 CONC ained glass. (Source: Clyde Wetteland at Wikitree)
2 CONT
