1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Erick, as a youth, was employed steamboating on the Missouri River.  In 1878, he purchased (and later homesteaded) a farm west of Hurley, SD.  He was among the first to set up sorghum mills in the county.  He serve
2 CONC d in the SD House of Representatives from 1899-1902, and in the SD Senate from 1913-1916.  He was President of the Turner Co. Farmers Mutual Insurance Co. for over 25 years, and served on the Board of Augustana College for some ye
2 CONC ars.
