2 DATE 8 MAR 1949
2 PLAC St Paul, Ramsey, MN
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Newspaper Man, Author, Educator, and Politician
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Martin was a respected writer, lecturer, and educator.  He received degrees from the University of South Dakota, and the University of Wisconsin.  He was a teacher in the public schools of Deerfield, DeForest, and 
2 CONC Madison, WI, and in Minneapolis, MN (1898-1904).  He moved then into journalism, and was the editor of the Wisconsin State Journal (1904-05), the Star-Times of Hudson, WI (1905-07), the Fergus Falls (MN) Free Press (1907-21), and 
2 CONC did freelance writing for the Minneapolis Tribune and other papers (1921-28).  He served as Minnesota State Legislator from Otter Tail County (1917-18).  He was a lecturer for the University of Minnesota (1928-31), served as Execu
2 CONC tive Secretary to the Governor of Minnesota (1931-33), and was director of publicity and investigator for the Minnesota Railroad and Warehouse Commission (1933-1935).  He authored a number of books: The Saga of the Norsemen in Ame
2 CONC rica (1925), The Life of Knute Nelson (1926), The Life of Alexander Ramsey (1927), The New Canaan (a historical novel, 1932), and River of Life and Death (a novel, 1934).  He was in "Who's Who in America" in 1934-35.
2 CONT
