2 CONT During 1890-93, Ole and Mary resided in a small house on his father's farm where Mabel and Willis were born.  In 1894, Ole purchased a farm on the edge of Gayville, SD. and built a house which was still standing in 1993.  Ole farm
2 CONC ed and sold buggies, farm machinery, water pumps, etc. in a Gayville business.  He and his brother Henry contracted to build a network of drainage ditches in the lowland areas of their birth in Clay County, a controversial project
2 CONC  that bankrupted the two brothers.  
2 CONT   Ole served on the Gayville Board of Education for many years, and was a member of the 1899 South Dakota House of Representatives from Yankton Co. - member of the 1899 South Dakota House of Representatives from Yankton Co. - appa
2 CONC rently the only member born in South Dakota.
