2 CONT On May 24, 1874, Gabriel Sørensen / Vestly was [http://digitalarkivet.arkivverket.no/kb/dp/person/pd00000002184474 Sponsor] on the birth of his niece Gertrude Marte Marie to parents Søren Sørensen / Vestly and Justine Gabrielsdtr 
2 CONC / Vestly, in Lye prestegjeld, Time sokn.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Feb. 24, 1884 Gabriel Vestly of Stavanger, Handlmd, was [http://digitalarkivet.arkivverket.no/kb/dp/person/pd00000001779390# Sponsor] on the birth of his nephew Kristoffer to Søren Sørensen / Vestly and wife Justine Gabrielsdtr
2 CONC  / Vestly, in Lye prestegjeld, Time sokn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Another son born to Søren Sørensen / Vestly and Justine Gabrielsdtr in 1886 (Lye prestegjeld, Time sokn) was also named Gabriel Sørensen Vestly, indicating the 1884 son did not survive.  Gabriel b. 1886 was  [http://digitalarkivet
2 CONC .arkivverket.no/kb/kf/person/pk00000000267904 Confirmed] in 1901.  He became a doctor in Manly, Iowa, and died there ca. 1952.
2 CONT
2 CONT Per the Sep. 30, 1894 [http://digitalarkivet.arkivverket.no/kb/kf/person/pk00000000266609 record] of a Confirmation in Lye Prstrgj., Gabriel S[ørensen] Vestly had a daughter, Gunhild Gabrielsdtr [of] Garpestad, born at Byrne, Thim
2 CONC e Sogn, on June 4, 1880.  Her mother was Gabriel's "separated wife" Grete Jonsdtr [of] Garpestad.  She had another child, Gabriel, born [http://digitalarkivet.arkivverket.no/kb/dp/hending/hd00000000387872 June 1873] and [http://di
2 CONC gitalarkivet.arkivverket.no/kb/kf/person/pk00000000228049 Confirmed] in 1888).  At the time of Gabriel's 1873 birth, Grete Jonsdtr was called "married wife" and was living with Isak Isaksen of Egeland -- but he is marked in the bi
2 CONC rth record as "bachelor."
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gabriel Vestly (born Lye Parish)''' & Elen Andersen [Levardsdatter] (born in Stavanger) were married April 27, 1881 in Stavanger Domkirken.  Elen's father listed as Levard Danielsen on the [http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:kb_read
2 CONC ?idx_kildeid=5146&uid=ny&idx_side=-44 record] (Image #43).  Their children (see in MEDIA):  
