1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sopie Marie Olesdatter (1853-1906) aka Sophia Olesdatter, aka Sofia Olesdatter (b. June 6, 1853; Vanse, Farsund, Vest-Agder, Norway - d. July 9, 1924; Ålesund, Møre og Romsdal, Norway) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: She was the daughter of Ole Mattias Pedersen (1822-1914) and Thea Johanne Torstensdatter (1825-1865). Ole was the son of Peder Andreas Hansen (1790-1849) of Log; and Maren Sophia Olsdatter (1791-1868) of Gullestad. Thea w
2 CONC as the daughter of Torsten Christophersen; and Johanne Jacobsdatter. Ole was a baker in Farsund.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: She was born on June 6, 1853 in Farsund, Vest-Agder, Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptism: She was baptized on July 3, 1853 as "Marie Sofie" at Farsund parish in Farsund, Vest-Agder, Norway. Her parenst were listed as "Ole Mattias Pedersen" and "Tea Johanne Vetteland".
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings: Sophia's siblings included: Peder Mattias Olsen (1848-?) aka Peter Olsen; Teodor Johan Olsen (1849-?) aka Theodore Johan Olsen; Josette Terefia Olsdatter (1855-?) aka Joletta Teresa Olsdatter, who was born on November 09
2 CONC , 1855; Otto Olson (1858-1921) aka Ottan Olson, who was born on February 09, 1858, and emigrated to Chicago and married Hannah E. Hansen (1864-1936); Hannah Eline Olsdatter (1860-1938) aka Lena Olson, who was born February 13, 186
2 CONC 0 and emigrated to Chicago; Salmine Sophia Severine Pedersen (1862-1914) aka Salmine Olsdatter who was born March 27, 1862 and married John Edward Winblad (1856-1914) and emigrated to New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT Farsund, Norway: The family appeared in the 1865 Norway census living in Farsund at 39 and 40 Kirkegaden Street. Her father, Ole, was working as a baker and was already a widower. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: She married Sigvard Nilsen I (1852-1906) on December 15, 1874 in Ålesund, Møre og Romsdal, Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: Peder Theodor Johan Nilsen (1874-?) was born on December 29, 1874 in Ålesund. This was just 14 days after his parents married. In 1880 Sigvard Nilsen I was born.
2 CONT
2 CONT Trondheim: By 1900 she and her husband were living in Trondheim, Norway. Her son, Sigvard Nilsen II (1880-?) was studying music in Berlin and was listed as "Sigvard Høhg-Nilsen". Peder Theodor Johan Nilsen (1874-?) doesn't appear 
2 CONC in the census, he is either living on his own, or dead.
2 CONT
2 CONT Widow: In 1910 was living with her father in Farund and she is receiving a pension as a widow.
2 CONT
2 CONT Postcard: On January 15, 1910, Sopie wrote to her neice in the US, Maria Elisabeth Winblad (1895-1987), the following, which has been translated from Norwegian into English: "Miss Maria Winblad, New York. Dear Niece Marie, Aunt So
2 CONC fie would now like to send you her and Grandfather's New Year's greetings and everything good in this year is wished to you; greetings to Tony." Sopie wrote Salmine Sophia Severine Pedersen (1862-1914), her sister around 1910-1913
2 CONC  the following: "A little post to you from your sister, stay well. Our most beloved dear Salmine and family, now when Sofie shall travel on Saturday, she will be kind and go to you and bring regards from your dear father and siste
2 CONC r, I have no address, as I get the letters in return, got a letter from Lina 8 days ago, she is good and sound and has visited you, sister, and she said you were in good mood and happy, yes God helps you and your people, so that y
2 CONC ou still may come to see your old father he is pretty well and was glad he heard that Lina think about a trip home, together with you if everything goes well, with the help of God, we live well, have no suffer. Marie Klungeland is
2 CONC  a candidate for confirmation October 6th. You John get regards from Malla Bekkevig Liva mm (with more). Dear be careful so that you once again can see old Norway, Lina wrote that she had a good time by Inga it was so nice, we hav
2 CONC e had a cold summer so we have had fire in the stove all the time, you shall get letters when I get A?a, love from father sister." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: She died on July 9, 1924 in Ålesund, More og Romsdal, Norway and is presumed to be buried there.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Researched and written by Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ) for Findagrave starting on September 15, 2003. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Updates: Updated on January 12, 2011 with additional information from Harald Søren Storaker (1951- ) of Norway with her death date and information from the 1900 and 1910 census.
