1 OCCU Barber
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Otto Olson (1858-1921) aka Ottan Olsen; aka Otto Olsen; Emigrated from Norway to Chicago, Illinois in 1877 and worked as a Barber (b. February 09, 1858, Vanse parish, Farsund, Vest-Agder, Norway - d. April 12, 1921
2 CONC , 465 Milwaukee Avenue, Chicago, Cook County, Illinois, USA)
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth:
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto was born in 1858 to Ole Mattias Pedersen (1820-1914) who worked as a baker; and Thea Johanne Torstensdatter (1825-1865) who may have died in childbirth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptism:
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto was christened under the name "Otan Olesen" in Vanse parish on March 21, 1858.
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings:
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto's siblings include: Peder Mathias Olsen (1851-?); Theodore Johan Olsen (1852-?); Sopie Marie Olsdatter (1852-after1908); Josette Theresa Olsdatter (1855-?) aka Joletta Olsdatter; Lena Elaine Olson (1860-1938) aka Hannah Eline
2 CONC  Olsdatter, who emigrated to Chicago in Illinois in the United States, and married Andrew Jensen (1861-1930); and the youngest was Salmine Sophia Pedersen (1862-1914) aka Salmine Sopie Severine Olsdatter, who married John Edward W
2 CONC inblad (1856-1914) and emigrated to New York City in the United States.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death of Mother:
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto's mother, Thea, died at a young age and Ole raised the seven living children alone. Ole never remarried.
2 CONT
2 CONT Farsund, Norway:
2 CONT
2 CONT The family was listed in the 1865 Norway Census living in Farsund.
2 CONT
2 CONT Emigration:
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto emigrated to the United States in 1877 and he lived in Chicago and worked as a barber. He may have appeared in the 1880 US Census living in Praire Farm, Barron County, Wisconsin, or this may be another Otto Olson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage:
2 CONT
2 CONT On September 04, 1884, under the name "Ottan Olsen" he married "Hannah E. Hansen" (1864-1936) at Our Saviour Lutheran Church in Chicago. Their marriage certificate was number "57254".
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Together they had the following children: Tille Olson (1885-1918) who married Norval Wintrone (1890-1918) and they both died along with their child in the influenza pandemic of 1918; Harry Oliver Olson (1887-1964) who served as a 
2 CONC Lieutenant in World War I, married a French woman named Germaine X (1900-1920) who died after two years of marriage in San Francisco, and they had no children; Mabel Olson (1890-1971) who married Jesse Garrett Clay (1888-1976) and
2 CONC  had one child and four grandchildren; Norman Otto Olson (1895-1977) who married Isabelle Wickman (1901-1931) and had one child, then he married Eva Folkert (1904-2000) from Germany and had three children; and Helen Olive Olson (1
2 CONC 900-1970) who married John Lozinski (1896-1980) and after a divorce married Frank Kirpichoff (1891-1965).
2 CONT
2 CONT Barber:
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto was listed in the 1880-1890 Chicago City Directory as a barber, working or living at 183 Milwaukee Avenue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Trip to Norway:
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1897 Otto was visiting his family in Norway. On August 20, 1897 he left from Kristiansand to return to Chicago and he was listed as a barber on the ship's manifest.
2 CONT
2 CONT Chicago, Illinois:
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1900 Otto and Hannah were living at 167 Milwaukee Avenue in Chicago and appear in the US Census.
2 CONT
2 CONT Postcard:
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto wrote a postcard to his sister, Salmine, and her husband John Winblad on December 25, 1908 and it read as follows: "Mr. John Winblad, 437 Wayne Street, Jersey City, New Jersey, USA, We thank our God, that we're not homeless t
2 CONC his Christmas, in snow and storm and slush. Merry Christmas and Happy New Year from your affectionate brother, Otto Olson". The postcard was postmarked from Chicago, Illinois. This postcard began the search for Otto's descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT Coal Dealer:
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1910 Chicago City Directory Otto was listed as a coal dealer working at 452 North Union; and as a barber at 465 Milwaukee Avenue, while living at 465 Milwaukee Avenue for both entries. The coal business appears to have not 
2 CONC lasted long.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death of Sister:
2 CONT
2 CONT His sister Salmine, died of a heart attack on December 18, 1914 while she was visiting Farsund.
2 CONT
2 CONT Chicago, Illinois:
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1917 Otto was again listed in the Chicago City Directory as a barber living and working at 465 Milwaukee Avenue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death:
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto died in 1921 of "chronic disease of the heart with chronic nephritis" while he was living at 465 Milwaukee Avenue in Chicago. Otto's death certificate incorrectly lists his birth year as "1857". It is listed as 1858 in his ba
2 CONC ptism record at Vanse parish in Farsund, Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial:
2 CONT
2 CONT He was buried in Mount Olive Cemetery at 3800 North Narragansett Avenue in Chicago.
2 CONT
2 CONT Widow:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah died on April 24, 1936 and was buried next to him on April 27, 1936.
2 CONT
2 CONT Legacy:
2 CONT
2 CONT There are four extant lines descending from Otto: Tille; Mabel; Norman; and Helen. Otto also had a sister, Lena living in Chicago, but the families drifted apart after Otto's death, so that by 2003 only Hazel Wintrone (1916- ) rem
2 CONC embered the Jensen side of the family in Chicago. On June 19, 2004, Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ) visited Dorothy Lozinski (1920- ) in Chicago. Dorothy is a grand-daughter of Otto. Otto had two cousins that came over from Farsund
2 CONC : Jakob E. Willumsen (1853-1928) who settled in Minnesota; and Inga Pedersen (1885-1927) who married Emil Schneider (c1880-1955) and lived in Jersey City, New Jersey. Jacob Willumsen left his children behind in the US and returned
2 CONC  to Norway after his wife died. There is a photo of him and one of his barber shop, but they may have been lost when they were send out to be used in a family video.
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationship:
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto Olson (1858-1921) was the great-granduncle of Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ). Otto was the grandfather of Dorothy Lozinski (1920- ) and Hazel Wintrone (1916- ). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT Researched and written by Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ) for Findagrave and loaded here at Geni.com on October 4, 2009.
