1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Edna Hilgerson Peterson Memorial Photos Flowers Edit Share Learn about sponsoring this memorial... Birth: 	Aug. 19, 1915 Clermont Fayette County Iowa, USA Death: 	Nov. 14, 2008 West Union Fayette County Iowa, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Edna Peterson, 93, of West Union, died Friday, Nov. 14, at Good Samaritan Home, West Union, of age-related causes.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born Aug. 19, 1915, at home near Clermont, daughter of Andrew and Helga Lerbold Hilgerson. She married Lenferd Peterson on July 24, 1938, in West Union. He died in July 1990.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Peterson worked several years as a hired girl, then later she and her husband farmed for many years near Castalia. She was a member of St. Olaf Lutheran Church, West Union.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survived by: a daughter, Shirley (Lawrence) Kohls of Clermont; a son, Kermit (Shirley) of Charles City; six grandchildren; 11 great-grandchildren; a stepgreat-grandchild; two sisters, Thelma Schweinefus of Ossian and Arlene Sutter
2 CONC  of West Union; and a brother, Adrian Hilgerson of Auburn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Preceded in death by: four sisters; and four brothers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services: 11 a.m. Tuesday at First Lutheran Church, Ossian, with burial in God's Acres Cemetery, Clermont. Public visitation from 4 to 7 p.m. today at Burnham-Wood Funeral Home, West Union. 
2 CONT
