1 NOTE {geni:about_me} barn		Gjertrud Marte Marie Westlye	29.04.1874:  http://digitalarkivet.arkivverket.no/kb/dp/person/pd00000002184468
2 CONT
2 CONT Immigrated 1894, naturalized 1909 [1920 Cavalier Co., ND census]
2 CONT
2 CONT * Lived 1900: Swan Lake, Turner Co., SD
2 CONT * Lived 1910: Spruce, Roseau Co., MN
2 CONT * Lived 1920: Storlie, Cavalier Co., ND (next to cousin Iver Iverson)
2 CONT * Lived 1930: Hampden, Ramsey Co., ND
2 CONT * Lived 1950: Hampden, Ramsey Co., ND [Obit of brother Søren]
2 CONT
2 CONT The first Homemakers Club in this community [Hampden] was organized March 20, 1935, with 18 members.  The officers were Mrs. Clarence Hedlund, president;  Mrs. O.W. Neidlinger, vice president;  Mrs. Glenn (Helen) Neidlinger, secre
2 CONC tary, and Mrs. Carl Mortenson, treasurer.  Other members were Mrs. L.O. Flott, Mrs. Henry Reimer, Mrs. Palmer Freed, Mrs. Ted Taylor, Mrs. M.A. Knutson, Miss Selma Hosterman, Mrs. Pete Rudser, Mrs. Norman Hoiland, Mrs. Dale Robert
2 CONC s, '''Mrs. Theodore Olson''', Mrs. Jerry Bragg, Mrs. W.L. Howe, Mrs. E.A. Neidlinger, and Miss Emma Waade.[https://hampden.wordpress.com/author/dakota1980/page/5/]
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruby Jenny (Norby) Olson was born August 25, 1915 at Kintyre, ND to Jon and Selma Norby.  Ruby was 5 years old when her mother passed away.  She was then '''legally adopted by Theodore and Gertrude Olson''' of Hampden, ND.   --Rub
2 CONC y Parker | 1915 - 2013 | Obituary  [https://www.meaningfulfunerals.net/home/index.cfm/obituaries/view/fh_id/14929/id/2724873]
