1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gunleiv Vestly in [https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:NWFW-SFS Norway, Baptisms 1634-1927]:
2 CONT * Birth Date:	28 Jun 1889
2 CONT * Christening Date:	28 Jul 1889
2 CONT * Christening Place:	Stavanger, Rogaland, Norway
2 CONT * Father's Name:	Gabriel Sørensen Vestly, b. 1849
2 CONT * Mother's Name:	Elen Levardsdatter, b. 1852
2 CONT * Original record is in ''SAST, Domkirken sokneprestkontor, Ministerialbok nr. A 29, 1889-1902, s. 2,  fødte og  døpte'' [births & baptisms] [https://media.digitalarkivet.no/view/5145/26590/3 '''Image 297 Listeside 3'''] (see in M
2 CONC EDIA).
2 CONT
2 CONT In ''Stavanger Aftenblad'', [http://www.nb.no/nbsok/nb/64894ba84549255923ddb210de03800a?index=35 October 24, 1906], age 17, at the bazaar of the "Teetotalers' Association."
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1919, at birth of first son, [http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:kb_read?idx_kildeid=1752&uid=ny&idx_side=-84 Reidulf Hess Westlye], Gunleif was "Hustømmermand" -- (house) carpenter."
2 CONT
2 CONT Atlantic crossings:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Gun'''t'''eif Westl'''ey''' (salesman) arrived New York Feb. 8, 1907 on the D/S ''Baltic'' out of Liverpool, age 17 yrs 7 mos [by that date he was 18 yrs, 7 mos], with $20, heading for Lakota, Nelson Co., N.D.  On the FamilySear
2 CONC ch.org version of the [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-C95S-Z9NK-Y?i=508&cc=1368704 '''ship's manifest'''], he is mis-indexed as WESTLEG.  The "relative or friend" Gunleif was going to join was "cousin [https://ww
2 CONC w.geni.com/people/S%C3%B8ren-Sam-Rimestad/6000000029058103222 '''Søren Rimestad'''], Hampden, Ramsey Co., ND" (see image in MEDIA; line 14).  Gunleif was traveling with two Rimestads, Sofie (22, servant) and Søren (30, farmer; Ame
2 CONC rican citizen).  Sofie & Søren (manifest lines 10 & 11) were Gunleif's first cousins; Søren (aka Sam Iverson) had immigrated in 1890 per the [https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:MLGP-Y71 '''1930'''] census.  (Two brothers of S
2 CONC ofie & Søren, [https://www.geni.com/people/Martin-Rimestad/6000000029059714049 '''Martin Rimestad'''] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Gilbert-Iverson-born-Gabriel-Iversen-Rimestad/6000000029063327425 '''Gabriel Rimestad'''] (=Gil
2 CONC bert Iverson), also went to Lakota, N.D. and appear with Søren/Sam on the 1910 census, along with Gunleif, called Gust.)  
2 CONT
2 CONT # Gunleif's 1907 departure from Stavanger is documented in [http://da.digitalarkivet.no/nn-no/gen/vis/8/pe00000000364313 Emigrantar over Stavanger 1903-1928''']: Gunleif Westly, departure date Jan. 25, 1907. The "Baltic" was a pos
2 CONC t- and passenger-ship of 24,000 tons in the fleet of Hvide Stjerne Linjen, a Norwegian line [http://www.nb.no/nbsok/nb/464552cde391d5cababbf607f962aec9?index=17 advertising] itself in Stavanger [http://www.nb.no/nbsok/nb/5c4d01064
2 CONC 5e3b9426f3371249a937e8b?index=25 newspapers] as "the shortest and fastest way" to America or to England (''Flash'' required to view the newspapers). 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Gunleif also appears on the ship's manifest for the ''Baltic'', White Star Line, sailing in March 1910 from Liverpool ''to New York,'' age 21, Laborer (see in MEDIA; yellow sheet).  No names provided for ''who going to.''
2 CONT
2 CONT # Gunleif returned to Norway ca. 1912 (the year his father died), was married there in 1916, then went back to New York in 1923.  On his  [https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:JNQN-FMN return to New York] (via Ellis Island), he
2 CONC  stated he had been in the US/ North Dakota from 1907-1912:
2 CONT * Gunleif Westlye, arrival date 1 May 1923.  
2 CONT * Birth Date:	abt 1890, Norway, Stavanger.
2 CONT * Age:	33.  Port of Departure:	Stavanger
2 CONT * Port of Arrival:	New York.
2 CONT * Ship Name:	''Stavangerfjord''
2 CONT * Occupation: Policeman.
2 CONT * Destination:  Ragnvald Staurnes Giske, brother-in-law, 649-48th St., Brooklyn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Year: 1923; Arrival: New York, New York; Microfilm Serial: T715; Microfilm Roll: 3289; Line: 26; Page Number: 56.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunleif had married [https://www.geni.com/people/Ingeborg-Staurnes-Hess-Westlye/6000000013283099516 '''Ingeborg Hess'''] (dau. of Jonas Didriksen Staurnes) in Stavanger, Norway, on December 7, 1916.  The wedding took place in Stav
2 CONC anger Domkirken; see image [http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:kb_read?idx_kildeid=1793&uid=ny&idx_side=-120 #116] (from [http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:kb_read Norwegian Digital Archive] Scanned Church Books: Rogaland, Prestegjeld Stav
2 CONC anger Domkirken ''Ministerialbok'' 1905-1922).
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1927, when Ingeborg and two sons followed him to New York, Gunleif was living at 52 Colonial Ave., Freeport, Long Island.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the [https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:X4N5-BJ6 '''1930'''] US Census for Brooklyn, NY (227 45th St. at 5th Ave; rented at $55/mo.):
2 CONT * ''Household	Role	Gender	Age	Birthplace''
2 CONT * Gunlief Westlye	Head	M	41	Norway (carpenter/construction)
2 CONT * Ingeborg Westlye	Wife	F	36	Norway
2 CONT * Reidulf Westlye	Son	M	11	Norway
2 CONT * Odd Westlye	Son	M	9	Norway
2 CONT * Carl Thalen	Lodger	M	35	Sweden (carpenter/construction)
2 CONT
2 CONT In the [https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:KQRW-SPL '''1940'''] US Census for Brooklyn, NY as '''Gunlrif Westley''':
2 CONT * ''[https://familysearch.org/pal:/MM9.3.1/TH-1971-27834-9835-49?cc=2000219 Household] ('''882 Fifth Avenue, Brooklyn''')	Role	Gender	Age	Birthplace''
2 CONT * Gunleif Westley	Head	M	50	Norway (carpenter, building construction)
2 CONT * Ingeborg Westley	Wife	F	44	Norway
2 CONT * Readulf Westley	Son	M	21	Norway (bookkeeper, savings bank)
2 CONT * Odd Westley	Son	M	19	Norway (clerk, telegraph off.)
2 CONT * Elinor Westley	Daughter	F	9	New York
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1942, Gunleif [https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:F36L-2JD registered] for the World War II draft, stating he resided at 483 79th Street, Brooklyn and worked with Marine Basin Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==============================================================
