1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Birth: 	Dec. 4, 1879, Stavanger, Rogaland fylke, Norway
2 CONT * Immigrated to U.S. in 1901, per the [https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:X4RB-NKR '''1930'''] U.S. census for Orange Co., New York.  See also [https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:33SQ-GRKZ-1YV?mode=g&i=7&wc=QZZH-QC9%3A13
2 CONC 3641301%2C134807401%2C143992601%2C1589088942%3Fcc%3D1727033&cc=1727033 1910 census] and 1914 [https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-89XQ-PB3B?i=894&wc=3XZZ-JWL%3A1056306501%2C1056626601%3Fcc%3D2185145&cc=2185145 passport ap
2 CONC plication].
2 CONT * Death: 	Feb. 23, 1962, Brooklyn, Kings Co., New York ([http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=96327216 '''FindAGrave''']
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Obituary:''  Port Jervis, NY. - Funeral services will be held Monday for Mrs. Inga Severine Coddington, formerly of Port Jervis, who died Friday in Brooklyn after a short illness. She was 83.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born Dec. 4, 1879, in Stavanger, Norway, the daughter of Sven and Fina Westlye. She was married Sept. 19, 1908 to George Coddington, who died in 1961. [He was 4 years older than Inga; 1930 census.]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was an employee of the Hotel Huguenot for many years.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by two brothers, Carl Westlye, of Calif., and Ingolf Westlye of Houston, Texas; several grand-nieces and nephews.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Rev. Robert Reich will conduct funeral services. Burial will be at Westbrookville.
2 CONT
2 CONT --The Times Herald-Record (Middletown, NY), Monday, February 26, 1962, page 37 
