1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jennie Marie Olsen (1881-1966) was a housewife. (b. May 1881; Chicago, Illinois - d. April 3, 1966; Grosse Pointe, Michigan)
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Anne Marie Jensen (1854-1896) of Farsund, Norway; and Peter Matthias Olsen (1849-1896) of Farsund, Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings: Osborne Theomun Olsen (1883-1971) aka Asbjorn T. Olsen, aka Ossie Olsen, owner of Osborne Art Studios in Chicago who married Augusta Schmidt (1883-1974) aka Gussie Schmidt; Perry Maranius Olsen (1885-1972) who moved to O
2 CONC akland, California; and Harriet Olsen (1889-?) who was born in March of 1889.
2 CONT
2 CONT Events: Jennie was a survivor of the SS Eastland, a passenger ship based in Chicago and used for tours. On July 24, 1915 the ship rolled over while loading passengers on a charter company picnic for the Western Electric Company. A
2 CONC  total of 844 passengers and crew were killed, the largest loss of life from a single shipwreck on the Great Lakes. Jennie survived, but her hair fell out and she wore wigs for the remainder of her life.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: She married Paul Henry Henning I (1881-1973) on June 24, 1916 in Chicago, Illinois.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: She died in Grosse Pointe, Michigan on April 3, 1966.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral notice: Her funeral notice appeared in the Chicago Tribune on April 6, 1966: "Henning. Jennie M. Henning, April 3, at Detroit, wife of Paul H.; mother of Paul H. Jr.; sister of Osborne T., and Perry Olsen. Funeral at the V
2 CONC erheyden Funeral Home, 16300 Mack, Grosse Pointe, Mich., Wednesday, at 10 am Interment Thursday ..."
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationships: She was the Your first cousin two times removed of Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ). She was the great grandmother of Lisa Scheer Harper.
2 CONT
2 CONT Research: Researched and written by Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ) for Findagrave starting on March 10, 2006. Updated on March 9, 2012 with her correct death information for her and her husband. The information came from Lisa Sche
2 CONC er Harper.
