1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sigvart Høgh-Nilsen (1880-?) aka Sigvard Nilsen II, was a Norwegian pianist and composer. (b. April 29, 1880; Ålesund, Møre og Romsdal, Norway - d. unknown; Norway)
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Sigvart Nilsen I (1852-1906) and Sophie Marie Olesdatter Nilsen (1853-1924).
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: He was born on 29 April 1880 in Ålesund, Møre og Romsdal, Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptism: He was baptized on 30 May 1880 in Ålesund, Møre og Romsdal, Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Berlin: He was studying music in Berlin and was listed as "Sigvard Høhg-Nilsen" in the 1900 Norway census.
2 CONT
2 CONT Recitals: Franz Liszt, Ballde H-moll (January 26, 1904)  Franz Liszt, Ballde H-moll (April 15, 1904) Johannes Brahms, Rhapsodie H-moll opus 70 (1906) Richard Wagner, Träume, with Anna Jensen (1906) Franz Liszt, Franciskus Legende 
2 CONC (St. Franciskus et Paul marchant sur les flots) (1906)
2 CONT
2 CONT Compositions: 2 Deutsche Lieder nr. 1 Ich hab' im Traum geweinet (Heine). (1906)
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: He most likely died in Norway but the date of his death is not known.
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationship: Sigvart Høgh-Nilsen (1880-?) was the first cousin twice removed of Richard Arthur Norton (1958- )
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Researched and written by Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ) for Findagrave starting on January 29, 2011.
