1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hannah E. Hansen (1864-1936) aka Hanne Amundsen, emigrated from Norway in 1880. (b. February 1864, Oslo, Norway - d. April 24, 1936, Chicago, Cook County, Illinois, USA) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: Hannah was born in Oslo, Norway possibly to Amund Hansen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings: She had at least three other siblings that emigrated with her: Carrie Hanson who's daughter, May, married Eden T. Brekke (1893-1978); Ole C. Hanson (1870-?) who lived in Dallas, Barron County, Wisconsin and had several c
2 CONC hildren; and a sister who lived in Seattle, Washington. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: Hannah married Otto Olson (1858-1921) on September 04, 1884 in Chicago at Our Saviour's Lutheran Church at 138th Street and Wabash Avenue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: Together they had the following children: Tille Olson (1885-1918) who married Norval Wintrone (c1885-1918) in Wisconsin then she and her husband died in the influenza pandemic at Devil's Lake, North Dakota; Harry Oliver 
2 CONC Olson (1887-1964) who served as a Lieutenant in World War I, married a French woman named Germaine X (1900-1920) who died after two years of marriage in San Francisco and they had no children; Mabel Olson (1890-1971) who married J
2 CONC esse Clay (1888-1976) and had one child and four grandchildren; Norman Otto Olson (1895-1977) who married Isabelle Wickman (1901-1931) and had one child, Norman Olson II (1921-1967) aka Buddy Olson, who died under the name "Norman
2 CONC  Wickman" and was buried in the Catholic Cemetery in Chicago, then Norman senior married Eva X (1904-2000) from Germany and had three children; and Helen Olson (1900-1970) who married John Lozinski (1896-1980) and had two children
2 CONC , Dorothy Lozinski and John Lozinski then she married Frank Kirpichoff (1891-1965). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Chicago, Illinois: In 1900 Otto and Hannah were living at 167 Milwaukee Avenue, Chicago, Cook County, Illinois with their four children. On February 13, 1910 it appears that Hannah was returning from a trip to Scandanavia by way o
2 CONC f Liverpool, England aboard the ship "Campania".
2 CONT
2 CONT Death of husband: In 1921 her husband died and in 1930 Hannah, now a widow was living with her son, Harry, a widower; and Hazel Wintrone who was the daughter of Tille. They were living at 1227 Mozart Street in Chicago. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: Hannah died on April 24, 1936.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral notice: Her funeral notice was in the Chicago Tribune on Sunday April 26, 1936 read as follows: "Hannah Olson nee Admundsen, wife of the late Otto, beloved mother of the late Mrs. Tillie Wintrone, Harry, Mrs. Mabel Clay, N
2 CONC orman, Helen, and Hazel Wintrone. Funeral services Monday 1 p.m. at chapel 2906 Madison Street. Interment Mount Olive."
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: She was buried on April 27, 1936 at Mount Olive Cemetery at 3800 North Narragansett Avenue in Chicago in the same plot as her husband Otto. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Research: Her death certificate needs to be ordered so that her parent's names can be determined.
