1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tillie Olson (1885-1918) aka Matilda Olson; Private Secretary at O'Connor and Goldberg Shoe Store in Chicago; Homesteader in Devil's Lake in North Dakota; Died during Influenza Pandemic of 1918-1919 (b. July 1885, 
2 CONC Chicago, Cook County, Illinois, USA - d. 1918, Devils Lake, Ramsey County, North Dakota, USA) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: Tillie was the daughter of Otto Olson (1857-1921) a barber born in Farsund, Norway and Hannah E. Hansen (1864-1936) born in Oslo, Norway. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings: Her siblings include: Harry Oliver Olson (1887-1964) who married Germaine X (1900-1920); Mabel Olson (1890-1971) who married Jesse Clay (1888-1976); Norman Otto Olson (1895-1977) who married Isabelle Wickman (1901-1931) 
2 CONC and after her death married Eva Folkerts (1904-2000); and Helen Olive Olson (1900-1970) who married John Lozinski (1896-1980). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Chicago: In Chicago Tillie worked in an office in the O'Connor and Goldberg shoe store as a private secretary. The economist Milton Friedman worked at the same store in 1932. Tillie appeared in the 1900 US Census living at 147 Mil
2 CONC waukee Avenue in Chicago, Illinois. In the 1910 Chicago City Directory she is listed as a "clerk" working at 262 5th Avenue and living at 465 Milwaukee Avenue. Tillie's family would visit her mother's siblings in Dallas, Wisconsin
2 CONC . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: She married Norval Wintrone on March 26, 1913 in Chicago, Cook County, Illinois. Norval chose to become a homesteader in Devil's Lake, North Dakota, so he would not have to serve in World War I. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: Tille and Norval died within a few days of each other during the influenza pandemic of 1918-1919. Their youngest child also died. The influenza epidemic of 1918 killed 2,700 North Dakotans.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hazel: Hazel Wintrone, her surviving daughter was then raised, first, by Hannah Hansen and later by Jesse Clay and Mabel Olson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Tillie and Norval are buried in the New Scandinavia Cemetery in Wisconsin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationship: Tillie Olson (1885-1918) was the first cousin, twice removed of Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ).
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Researched and written by Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ) for Findagrave starting on September 25, 2005. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Updates: Updated with their marriage date and location on July 16, 2011 by Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ).
