1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mabel Olson (1890-1971) Clerk and Housewife (b. June 25, 1890, Chicago, Cook County, Illinois, 60619, USA - d. August 15, 1971, Rockford, Winnebago County, Illinois, USA) Social Security Number 329449523.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mabel was the daughter of Otto Olson (1857-1921) a barber born in Farsund, Norway; and Hannah E. Hansen (1864-1936).
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings:
2 CONT
2 CONT Her siblings include: Tillie Olson (1885-1918) who married Norval Wintrone (1890-1918) and died in the influenza pandemic; Harry Oliver Olson (1887-1964) who served in World War I and later married Germaine X (1900-1920); Norman O
2 CONC tto Olson (1895-1977) who married Eva Folkerts (1904-2000) and after a divorce married Isabelle Wickman (1901-1931); and Helen Olson (1900-1970) who married John Joseph Lozinski I (1896-1980) and later divorced.
2 CONT
2 CONT Chicago:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mabel appears in the 1900 US Census in Chicago living with her parents at 167 Milwaukee Avenue. She appeared in the 1910 Chicago City Directory working as a clerk and living at 465 Milwaukee Avenue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marrige:
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Jesse Garrett Clay (1888-1976) around 1911.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child:
2 CONT
2 CONT They had one child: Harry Garrett Clay (1913-1965).
2 CONT
2 CONT Rockford, Illinois:
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1930 Jesse and Mabel were living at 1611 Myott S. Sherman Street in Rockford and Jesse was working as a railroad postal clerk. They owned their own home and it was valued at $6,250.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mabel died in 1971 and was buried in Willwood Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary:
2 CONT
2 CONT Her obituary from the Chicago Tribune is as follows: "Services for Mrs. Mabel Clay, 81, of 2202 Logan Street, Rockford, will be held at 3 p.m. today in the chapel at 304 North 5th Avenue, Rockford. Mrs. Clay died Friday in a Rockf
2 CONC ord nursing home. Mrs. Clay, who was born in Chicago, spent most of her life in Rockford. She leaves her husband, Jesse; three grandsons; seven great-grandchildren; and a brother."
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationship:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mabel Olson (1890-1971) was the first cousin, twice removed of Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ).
