1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alvin Jensen (1899-1986) aka Ab Jensen; Clerk at Continental and Commercial National Bank in 1917; Later a Worker at Brach's Candy (b. July 18, 1899, Chicago, Cook County, Illinois, USA - d. July 1986, Phoenix, Mar
2 CONC icopa County, Arizona, 85018, USA) Social Security Number 335056773. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: Alvin was the son of Andrew Havig Jensen (1861-1930) and Lena Elaine Olsen (1860-1938) aka Hannah Eline Olsdatter. Alvin was born at home with a midwife, which may contribute to the problem of determining his correct birthd
2 CONC ay. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings: His siblings include: Mary (Marie) Jensen (1883-1969) who was married to Albert Rath (1881-1950) and later married Nels Hemwall; Thea Jensen (1885-1910) who married Max Caro (1882-1918); Leif Jensen (1886-1955) who marri
2 CONC ed Agnes Hansen (1890-1965); Leonard George Jensen I (1887-1979) who married Gertrude Brock (1892-1944); Josetta (Dolly) Dorothy Jensen (1889-1940) who married William James Gogerty (1893-1939); Margerite (Daisy) Jensen (1891-1986
2 CONC ) who married Francis (Frank) Joseph Woods (1891-1972); Sally (Goldie) Jensen (1893-1965) who married William Holm (1891-1983); Eleanore Margaret Jensen (1897-1987) who married Mahlon Edward Shanahan (1900-1993). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Chicago, Illinois: In the 1917 Chicago City Directory Alvin is listed as working as a clerk at the Continental and Commercial National Bank, and living at 4940 West Austin Avenue. 
2 CONT
2 CONT World War I draft: Alvin registered for the draft for World War I on September 12, 1918 while he was living at 4940 West Austin Avenue in Chicago. He listed his birthday as "July 18, 1900", not the "July 18, 1899", which is the bi
2 CONC rth recorded by Social Security. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: Alvin married Helen Mae Baldwin (1907-1998) around 1929.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: They had the following children: an un-named girl Jensen (1929) who died at birth; Alvin Edward Jensen (1931-1995) who married Shirley (1935- ); and William Jensen. Alvin worked for short periods at many different jobs. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation: Alvin worked at Brach's Candy in Chicago, as did his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: He retired to Arizona where he died in 1986. His widow returned to Chicago after his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Memories of Alvin Jensen: Maureen Elizabeth Donahue (1937- ) said: "Alvin was friends with his first cousin Otto Perry Winblad (1902-1977), and he visited him in New Jersey, and they exchanged letters which may still exist in Chic
2 CONC ago." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationship: Alvin Jensen (1899-1986) was the first cousin, twice removed from Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ).
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Researched and written by Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ) for Findagrave starting on April 10, 2004. 
