1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Edward Winblad II (1897-1899), aka Eddie Winblad, who died as an infant of pneumonia. (b. August 28, 1897, 437 Wayne Street, Jersey City, Hudson County, New Jersey, 07307, USA - d. September 24, 1899, 437 Wayn
2 CONC e Street, Jersey City, Hudson County, New Jersey, 07307, USA) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth:
2 CONT
2 CONT Eddie was the child of John Edward Winblad I (1856-1914) of Sweden; and Salmine Sophia Severine Pedersen (1861-1914) of Farsund, Norway. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings:
2 CONT
2 CONT His siblings include: Anton Julius Winblad (1886-1975) aka Tony Winblad; Theodora Winblad (1888) who died as an infant; Mary Winblad (1889) who died as an infant, Otto Edward Winblad (1892); Marie Elizabeth Winblad (1895-1987) aka
2 CONC  Mae Winblad, who married Arthur Oscar Freudenberg (1891-1968); and Otto Perry Winblad (1902-1977). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death:
2 CONT
2 CONT He died of "bronchio pneumonia" at the age of two years and one month, after two weeks of illness. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Memories about John Edward Winblad II:
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ) writes on January 07, 2008: My grandmother, Marie Elizabeth Winblad (1895-1987), called him "Eddie", and said he had died when he was just a few years old. She had my sister take her to go look for h
2 CONC is grave, but I don't think they found it that day. Marie, eventually would be buried in the same plot with her brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Legacy:
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Winblad, his sister would visit his grave throughout her life and was buried next to him at her own request.
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationship:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Edward Winblad II (1897-1899) was the granduncle of Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ), although he died as an infant.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT Researched and written by Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ) for Findagrave starting on July 14, 2003.
