1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/75471644/rita_louise_odland
2 CONT
2 CONT RITA LOUISE ODLAND
2 CONT (January 8, 1933 - August 25, 2010)
2 CONT
2 CONT Rita Louise Odland, age 77, long-time Menahga, MN resident, passed away peacefully at her home on Wednesday, August 25, 2010 surrounded by her loving daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rita was born January 8, 1933 to John and Mary (Courchane) Sangrey in Havre, Montana, the 4th born of 6 children. Rita grew up and attended school in White Sulfur Springs, MT graduating with the class of 1952. Rita was united in m
2 CONC arriage to Donald Odland on May 15th in 1953. This union was blessed with 4 daughters: Laurie, Lonnie, and Lita and Lecil. When her children reached school age, Rita gained employment at the Montana State University as a cook. In 
2 CONC 1972, the young family moved to Menahga, MN. Rita then gained employment at St. Joseph's Hospital in Park Rapids where she worked for a few years before attending Detroit Lakes Technical College where she received her License Prac
2 CONC tical Nursing Degree. She then began her career at Green Pine Acres Nursing Home in Menahga where she worked for 30 years before retiring.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Rita was not busy with her family and work, she enjoyed many hobbies. She was an avid reader, enjoyed a good game of cards, going to the casino, playing bingo and also enjoyed crafts such as sewing, crocheting, knitting and p
2 CONC ainting ceramics. During later years, Rita stayed busy with a Karaoke business that she operated with her sister-in-law, Lila Odland Savonto. She was a long-time member of First English Lutheran Church in Menahga and was a member 
2 CONC of the Menahga VFW Post #6206 Auxiliary.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rita will be dearly missed by her 4 daughters: Laurie (Steve) Skaro of Sebeka, Lonnie Odland of Park Rapids, Lita (Sheldon) Sagedahl of Menahga and Lecil (Matt) Miller of Menahga; 14 grandchildren; 19 great grandchildren; 3 sister
2 CONC s: Bernice Tony of Townsend, MT; Claira Boster of Townsend, MT, and Key (David) Kari of Lima, MT; many cousins, nieces, nephews other relatives and friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her parents John and Mary. Don Odland, 3 grandsons: Donnie Skaro, and Caden and Aiden Werlinger; sisters, Delephine and Jacqueline; and her brother, Elmer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held 1 PM, Monday, August 30, 2010 at First English Lutheran Church in Menahga with Reverend Steven A. Bruer officiating. Casketbearers will be: Son-in-laws Steve Skaro, Sheldon Sagedahl, Mathew Miller, an
2 CONC d Grand Children: Ryan Burkman, Chelsey Miller, Stephanie Vandermay, and Jennifer Sagedahl. Honorary casket bearers will be: all of her Grand Children and Great Grand Children. Interment will be made in Shell City Cemetery. Visita
2 CONC tion will be held Sunday, August 29, 2010 at 6 PM to 9 PM at First English Lutheran Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wevley Funeral Home, Sebeka, MN
