1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/42464280/lila_jane_suvanto
2 CONT
2 CONT Lila Jane (Odland) Suvanto, 68, of Menahga, died Tuesday, March 17, 2009 at Green Pine Acres Nursing Home in Menahga. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born on Feb. 27, 1941 to Henry and Elma (Stahl) Hepola in Menahga, where she was raised and attended school. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Linden Odland on Dec. 20, 1958. They had seven children.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a member of First English Lutheran Church in Menahga. She was a life member of the Menahga VFW, where she served as president, senior vice president, conductress and musician. She was also a member of the American Legion a
2 CONC nd Menahga Gateway Lions, where she was gambling manager. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On April 27, 2002 she married Alvin Suvanto. They lived in Menahga and spent winters in Mesa, Ariz.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by her husband, Alvin Suvanto; four sons: Lindy (Kristi), of Menahga, Gary, of Molalla, Ore., Oscar, of Park Rapids, and Andy, of Menahga; six sisters: Mary Ann Lindula, of Edgewood, Wash., Inga Palola, of Two Harb
2 CONC ors, Lempi (Jack) Molenda, of Arlington, Wash., Edna Roenneberg, of DeSoto, Wis., Irene Nordby, of Menahga, and Betty Turpin, of Helena, Mont.; a brothers, William Hepola, of Auburn, Wash.; and many grandchildren, great-grandchild
2 CONC ren and other relatives.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by two sisters: Aili and Amy; two daughters: Roxanne and Faye Dawn; and a son, Robert.
2 CONT
2 CONT Honorary casket bearers: All of her grandchildren, great-grandchildren, nieces, nephews and friends.
2 CONT Active casket bearers: Andy Bimberg, Aaron Fairbanks, Shawn Mattila, Eddie Lund, Kyle Odland and Duane Paulson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral service: 11 a.m. today (Saturday), March 21 at First English Lutheran Church in Menahga with Pastor Steven A. Bruer officiating. Shirley Anderson will serve as organist. Special music includes Romyn Hanks singing "The Danc
2 CONC e" and a recording of "Sissy's Song." Congregational hymns are "On Eagles Wings," "Amazing Grace" and "Just As I Am."
2 CONT Interment: Shell City Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Perham Focus online
